  <prompt>
    Add the triage output fields to the EXISTING `sprk_communication` entity so the triage Action (022/023) and the enrichment path (025) have somewhere to persist per-email triage state. This is ADDITIVE and non-breaking (NFR-04) — existing `sprk_communication` columns MUST stay exactly as-is. Per D-01 there is NO new triage entity — triage state hangs off `sprk_communication`.

    **VERIFY-OR-CREATE**: the operator may have pre-created some/all of these fields in a parallel schema pass. FIRST enumerate the live `sprk_communication` attributes via Dataverse MCP `describe`; for each field below, CREATE it only if missing, and if present, RECONCILE its type/target against this spec (flag any mismatch — do NOT silently retype an in-use field; escalate a type conflict). Add ONLY what is missing.

    Add, via the `dataverse-create-schema` skill patterns, the six triage fields (use Spaarke naming conventions; verify option-set integer conventions via MCP before creating any Choice):

    1. **`sprk_triagecategory`** — a **Lookup** to the category taxonomy config table `sprk_triagecategory` (the config table itself is task 013). If 013's table does not exist yet at create time, create the lookup against it once available OR record the dependency; the field is a categorization pointer, not a free-text category.
    2. **`sprk_triagepriority`** — priority (Choice or Whole Number per the priority-weight model; align with 013's priority-weight convention).
    3. **`sprk_triagesummary`** — the 2-line summary (multiline Text).
    4. **`sprk_triageobligations`** — extracted obligations as **lean JSON** (multiline Text holding a compact JSON array; D-06). Document the JSON shape in the task note for future promotion to child records (FR-07 acceptance).
    5. **`sprk_riconfidence`** — the RI-confidence score (Decimal, 0–1) computed by task 024.
    6. **`sprk_reviewoutcome`** — the review-outcome Choice (D-05: term "review outcome", NOT "disposition" — avoids the ADR-040 clash). Confirm the closed value set at task time (spec Assumptions: File / Update / Route / Dismiss + engine Suggested/Ambiguous statuses).

    Deploy to the project solution. This is schema ONLY — the scorer LOGIC is 024, the triage Action is 022/023, the persistence wiring is 025.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke Dataverse schema engineer. Fluent in the `dataverse-create-schema` skill (Web API + PowerShell for patterns PAC CLI can't do), additive/non-breaking schema evolution, and the D-01 "triage hangs off `sprk_communication`" decision. You add exactly the fields FR-07 names — nothing speculative — you never retype an in-use field, and you verify-before-create so an operator's parallel schema pass is reconciled, not duplicated.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `sprk_communication` gains the six triage fields (`sprk_triagecategory` lookup, `sprk_triagepriority`, `sprk_triagesummary`, `sprk_triageobligations` lean-JSON, `sprk_riconfidence` decimal, `sprk_reviewoutcome` choice) — all additive, existing columns untouched, verify-or-create reconciled against any operator-pre-created shape. The obligations JSON shape is documented for future child-record promotion. Tasks 024 (writes `sprk_riconfidence`) and 025 (persists category/priority/summary/obligations/reviewoutcome on the enrichment path) can build against real schema. No existing column retyped; the review-outcome term is "review outcome", never "disposition".
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      r1 activates the already-produced-but-dark AI classification and computes a real RI-confidence, persisting the results as triage state on `sprk_communication` (D-01 — no new `sprk_triageitem` entity). Today `sprk_communication` has the association/enrichment fields but no triage output fields, so the triage Action (022/023) and the RI-confidence scorer (024) have nowhere to write. This task adds them additively.

      §11 Component Justification (triage fields = new surface, but they EXTEND the entity per D-01): (1) **Existing overlap** — `sprk_associationstatus` exists but carries association state, not triage output (001 confirms no triage fields). (2) **Extension instead** — triage state extends `sprk_communication` (D-01); a new entity was explicitly rejected. (3) **Concrete cost-of-doing-nothing** — without these fields the triage Action has nowhere to persist category/summary/obligations/priority (Pillar 1 fails — success-criterion 4) and the RI-confidence scorer has nowhere to write the score (notification path stays dark — success-criterion 5). Named contract failures, not "future flexibility."

      The review-outcome field is deliberately named "review outcome" (D-05) to avoid ADR-040's ownership of "disposition" (ADR Tensions path-A exception). The obligations are lean JSON (D-06) — a compact array on the parent, documented for later promotion.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/001-operator-schema-verification.md (task 001 output — live `sprk_communication` attribute set; consume to know what already exists)</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/spec.md (FR-07, D-01/D-05/D-06, Assumptions → review-outcome value set)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Models/Ai/Communication/CommunicationClassificationResult.cs (the classification shape the triage output mirrors — category/summary/obligations/priority)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationEnrichmentService.cs (the path task 025 uses to persist into these fields)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-07 / NFR-04">Additive only. Add the six triage fields; MUST NOT alter or retype any existing `sprk_communication` column. Verify-before-create; reconcile (do not duplicate) any operator-pre-created field; escalate a type conflict rather than silently retyping an in-use field.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-01">Triage state hangs off `sprk_communication`. MUST NOT create a new `sprk_triageitem` (or any new triage) entity.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-05 (ADR-040 path-A)">The review-outcome field uses the term "review outcome" (`sprk_reviewoutcome`); MUST NOT reuse "disposition" (owned by ADR-040).</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-06">Obligations stored as lean JSON on `sprk_communication` (multiline Text); document the JSON shape in the task note for future child-record promotion. MUST NOT create per-obligation child rows in P1.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Verify option-set/lookup conventions via Dataverse MCP `describe`/`read_query` BEFORE creating any Choice/Lookup; do NOT guess integers from memory. `sprk_triagecategory` is a Lookup to the config table (task 013).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-027">Author schema into the project's managed solution per subscription-isolation/solution conventions; no direct prod-only unmanaged changes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Schema ONLY. No scorer logic (024), no triage Action (022/023), no persistence wiring (025), no BFF code.</constraint>
  </constraints>

