  <justification>
    <existing>`sprk_communication` has `sprk_associationstatus` (association state) but no triage-output fields; grep/MCP-confirmed by task 001. The category taxonomy is a separate config table (013).</existing>
    <extension>These fields EXTEND `sprk_communication` per D-01 (a new triage entity was explicitly rejected). No new entity; a lookup to the 013 config table plus five typed columns on the existing entity.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without these fields the triage Action (022/023) cannot persist category/summary/obligations/priority (Pillar 1 / success-criterion 4 fails) and the RI-confidence scorer (024) has nowhere to write the score, leaving the notification path dark (success-criterion 5 fails). Concrete contract failures, not scalability/flexibility.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read task 001's note (live `sprk_communication` attributes) + spec FR-07/D-01/D-05/D-06/Assumptions + `CommunicationClassificationResult.cs` to fix the exact fields + confirm the review-outcome closed value set and the obligations JSON shape.</step>
    <step order="2">Via Dataverse MCP `describe`, enumerate the live `sprk_communication` attributes; determine which of the six triage fields already exist (operator parallel pass) and which are missing; reconcile types for any present field (flag/ escalate a conflict, do NOT retype an in-use field).</step>
    <step order="3">Create ONLY the missing fields via `dataverse-create-schema`: `sprk_triagecategory` (Lookup → the 013 config table; record the dependency if 013 not yet created), `sprk_triagepriority`, `sprk_triagesummary` (multiline), `sprk_triageobligations` (multiline lean-JSON), `sprk_riconfidence` (Decimal 0–1), `sprk_reviewoutcome` (Choice, value set confirmed in step 1). Verify Choice integer conventions via MCP first.</step>
    <step order="4">Deploy the schema to the project solution. Verify a `sprk_communication` record accepts a value in each new field; confirm existing columns are unchanged and still readable.</step>
    <step order="5">Document the created-schema inventory (logical names, types, targets, the `sprk_reviewoutcome` value set, the `sprk_triageobligations` JSON shape) in `notes/011-triage-fields.md` for 025 + the §11 justification.</step>
    <step order="6">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (011 ✅) + `current-task.md`; confirm 025 unblocked and note the `sprk_triagecategory`→013 dependency.</step>
  </steps>

